Python is a high-level, general-purpose programming language created by
Guido van Rossum and first released in 1991. It is known for its clean,
readable syntax that uses indentation to define code blocks.
 
It is commonly used for 
    Web development (Django, Flask, FastAPI)
- Data analysis and visualization (pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib)
- Machine learning and AI (scikit-learn, PyTorch, TensorFlow)
- Automation and scripting
- Scientific computing
- Testing and DevOps tooling
